commit 3920542d549d865d299bcc9d3c3de2726d8e97be
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Wed Oct 28 08:37:49 2026 +1100

    Read config options where they are used, not at import
    
    objects/base.py, quotasv2.py and quotasv2_detail.py read options at
    import, so any tool that imports them before parsing its configuration,
    such as neutron-ovn-db-sync-util, sees the defaults. Read "debug" and
    "quota_driver" when they are used, and always register the ORM hook.
    
    quotasv2 compared the run-time driver with its own import-time value,
    so whether its description said "per project" depended on import
    order. It now checks the driver against QUOTA_DB_DRIVERS, a tuple of
    the two database drivers added to neutron.conf.quota.
    
    Assisted-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (high effort)
    Change-Id: Iebbb77f7b7190126973711100896c0fa1d487570
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

